        "ruleCards": [
          {
            "title": "Extra rules",
            "content": "Tahm Kench is a Large fighter (he can attack up to 2 spaces away).\n(With his ability, if he lands on a fighter, the fighter can be moved through opponents.) If the fighter has 3 fish markers they take 1 damage on impact.\nFish markers: if an opponent has 3 stacks of fish markers, some of your cards might have an extra effect. An opponent can have maximum 3 markers. Discarded markers go back to Tahm Kench."
          },
          {
            "title": "Devour",
            "content": "You can only play this card on opponents if there is at least one opponent that has 3 stacks. Choose an enemy hero with 3 stacks or an ally hero. Eat it. Remove it from the board.\nAt the start of their turn enemies can choose to: skip their turn, or have 1 action and take 5 damage, or have 2 actions and take 8 damage. After they chose, return them on a space of your choosing.\nIf you ate an ally, at the start of their turn they can choose: skip their turn and restore 8 health, or have 1 action and restore 3 health, or just start their turn normally. Return them to a space of your choosing."
          }
        ]
      }
